cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this file) and the
  accompanying paper listed under preferred-citation.
title: >-
  rare-property-retrieval: an enrichment-driven workflow for discovering
  materials with rare target properties
abstract: >-
  Code and workflow for enrichment-driven discovery of materials whose target
  property is rare and expensive to validate. A fine-tuned property regressor
  and a rare-class classifier on frozen pretrained embeddings are combined by
  reciprocal-rank fusion; diversity-aware and disagreement-aware nomination
  allocates a fixed budget of first-principles validations. Demonstrated on the
  retrieval of low-band-gap metal-organic frameworks confirmed with HSE06.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/EYErbil/Rare-Property-Retrieval-in-MOFs"
url: "https://github.com/EYErbil/Rare-Property-Retrieval-in-MOFs"
authors:
  - family-names: Erbil
    given-names: "Ege Yiğit"
    affiliation: "Koç University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5486-8111"
keywords:
  - rare-event retrieval
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - band gap
  - machine learning
  - reciprocal-rank fusion
  - density functional theory
  - HSE06
